       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. I can't verify the protocol or the pharmacist review. No recognized protocol uses sertraline at 1000 mg/day, and that is five times the labeled maximum. If the order is wrong, the patient could be seriously harmed, so I won't enter it on an unverified statement.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** For example, I can enter 100 mg or 200 mg by mouth once daily, or a starting dose of 25\u201350 mg. Tell me which one.\n- **Go through the pharmacist and prescriber.** If a protocol exists, the reviewing pharmacist and the prescriber of record can enter or co-sign the order directly. The system will then show their documentation and any required override. I can add a note for them if that helps.\n- **Check the source.** If the order came from a protocol or a handoff, please compare it against the original. A 10x error, such as 100 mg written as 1000 mg, is a common transcription mistake.\n\nWhich of these would you like me to do?"
      }
     ],
